📖 Surah Al-‘Ādiyāt (100)
______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

🌟 1. Background

Surah Al-‘Ādiyāt Makki surah hai, 11 ayaat par mushtamil hai.
Isme jang ke ghodon ki misaal di gayi hai jo shiddat se daudte hain.
Ye misaal insaan ko samjhane ke liye hai ke jis tarah ghoda apne malik ke liye wafadari dikhata hai, waise insaan ko bhi apne Rab ke liye shukriya ada karna chahiye.
Lekin insaan na-shukra hai, maal ka deewana hai aur Qayamat bhool jaata hai.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

🌟 2. Ayat by Ayat Translation

✅Ayah 1-5: Allah ki Qasmein

Wal-‘aadiyaati dabha, Fal-mooryaati qadha, Fal-mugheeraati subha, Fa-atharna bihi naq’a, Fawa satna bihi jam’a.

Tarjuma (Roman Urdu):
Qasam hai un ghodon ki jo zor zor se saans lete hue daudte hain.
Jinke khuron (hoof) se pathron par chingariyaan nikalti hain.
Jo subah ke waqt achanak dushman par hamla karte hain.
Jo dhool uda dete hain.
Aur dushman ki jama’at mein ghus jaate hain.

Tafseer:
Allah Ta’ala jang ke ghodon ki misaal de kar insaan ki tawajju dilata hai. 
Ghoda apne malik ke liye sab kuch karta hai – bhook, thakan, khatra bardasht karta hai. 
Lekin insaan, jise Allah ne sab kuch diya hai, apne Rab ka shukriya nahi karta.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

✅Ayah 6-8: Insaan ki Haqiqat

Innal-insaana li rabbihi la-kanood, Wa innahu ‘ala dhalika la-shaheed, Wa innahu li hubbil khairi la-shadeed.


Tarjuma (Roman Urdu):
Beshak insaan apne Rab ke liye bohot hi na-shukra hai.
Aur woh is baat par khud gawah hai.
Aur woh maal-o-daulat ki mohabbat mein sakht hai.

Tafseer:

Kanood ka matlab: Aisa shakhs jo milne wali ni’mat bhool jaye aur sirf mushkilat yaad rakhe.
Insaan Allah ki hazaron ni’maton ke bawajood shukriya ada nahi karta.
Uska dil maal se itna mohabbat rakhta hai ke woh Allah aur aakhirat bhool jaata hai.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
✅Ayah 9-11: Aakhirat ki Yaad

Afala ya’lamu iza bu’thira ma fil-quboor, Wa hussila ma fis-sudoor, Inna rabbahum bihim yawma’izil lakhabeer.

Tarjuma (Roman Urdu):
Kya insaan jaanta nahi ke jab qabron mein jo kuch hai woh nikaala jaayega?
Aur dilon mein jo kuch hai woh zahir kar diya jaayega.
Us din unka Rab unse khoob waaqif hoga.

Tafseer:

Qayamat ke din sirf zahiri a’maal nahi, balki dilon ke iradey, niyyaten aur raaz bhi khol diye jaayenge.
Insaan ki har harkat aur har soch Allah ke samne pesh ki jaayegi.
Us waqt maal ki mohabbat, duniya ki daulat kaam nahi aayegi.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

🌟 3. Lessons 

Shukriya ada karo – Har ni’mat Allah ki den hai, is liye na-shukri se bacho.
Maal ka asliyat samjho – Dunya ka maal sirf test hai, asal daulat akhirat hai.
Aakhirat ki tayyari – Har amal aur niyyat khol di jayegi, is liye saaf dil aur achi niyyat rakhni chahiye.
Wafadari – Ghoda apne malik ke liye wafadari karta hai, insaan ko apne Rab ke liye wafadari karni chahiye.
Hisaab ka din yaqini hai – Har raaz saamne aayega, kuch bhi chhupaya nahi jaa sakta.

